  "proof_summary": "For arbitrary rational quaternion parameters a,b, any two maximal integer orders Lambda1,Lambda2, every height-one place v containing a natural prime ell, and every split matrix ring equivalence phi preserving scalar matrices, retain one common natural e and both orientations of local-box normal form: an invertible h identifies the first box with integral 2-by-2 matrices and the second box with the conjugate by diag(1,ell^e), and an independently chosen invertible h-prime gives the reversed orientation using the same e. All equivalences range over every quaternion in the local tensor algebra. Preserve the full denominator-clearing, Cartan decomposition, frame conversion and symmetric flip proof; e=0 is retained and no extra ramification or coprimality assumption is added.",
